import IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Bridge
import IUT.Prerequisites.PadicVolume

/-!
# Normalized log-volumes on the rings of integers of finite extensions of `ℚ_p` and on tensor packets

Sources: Mochizuki, *Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory IV*, Proposition 1.1 (page 9 and the
proof on pages 9 and 10), Proposition 1.2 (pages 10 and 11), Proposition 1.4 (pages 13 and 14).
Pages read for this file: 8, 9, 10, 11, 13 and 14. Pages checked against rendered images: the
same. Displays relied on:
* page 9: `R_E = ⊗_{i ∈ E} R_i` over `ℤ_p`, `p ^ (𝔡_{I*}) · (R_I)^∼ ⊆ R_I ⊆ (R_I)^∼`, with
  `(−)^∼` "the normalization of the [reduced] ring in parentheses in its ring of fractions";
* page 10: "For `λ ∈ (1 / e_i) · ℤ`, we shall write `p ^ λ · R_i` for the fractional ideal of
  `R_i` generated by any element `p ^ λ` of `k_i` such that `ord(p ^ λ) = λ`"; Proposition 1.2 (i)
  `p ^ (a_i) · R_i ⊆ log_p(R_i^×) ⊆ p ^ (−b_i) · R_i`, equalities when `p > 2` and `e_i ≤ p − 2`;
  Proposition 1.2 (ii) `φ(p ^ λ · (R_I)^∼) ⊆ p ^ ⌊λ − 𝔡_I − a_I⌋ · log_p(R_I^×) ⊆
  p ^ (⌊λ − 𝔡_I − a_I⌋ − b_I) · (R_I)^∼`;
* page 13, Proposition 1.4 (i): `μ^log` is "normalized so that `μ^log(R_i) = 0`,
  `μ^log(p · R_i) = −log(p)`", and on tensor products, which "decompose, naturally, as direct sums
  of finitely many finite extensions of `ℚ_p`", "defined on compact open subsets of such tensor
  products" and "normalized so that `μ^log((R_E)^∼) = 0`, `μ^log(p · (R_E)^∼) = −log(p)`";
  Proposition 1.4 (ii) `μ^log(log_p(R_i^×)) = −(1 / e_i + m_i / (e_i f_i)) · log(p)`, with `p ^ (f_i)`
  the cardinality of the residue field and `p ^ (m_i)` the order of the `p`-primary part of the
  torsion of `R_i^×`;
* page 14: the computation `μ^log(p ^ ⌊λ − 𝔡_I − a_I⌋ · log_p(R_I^×)) ≤ (−λ + 𝔡_I + a_I + 1) ·
  log(p) + μ^log(log_p(R_I^×))`, which uses that multiplying by `p ^ ν` shifts `μ^log` by
  `−ν log(p)`. The formula `μ^log(p ^ λ · R) = −λ log p` proved below
  (`volBridge_muLog_fractionalIdeal`) is that scaling rule on one factor; it is not printed as a
  display on the pages read.

## The objects

As in `IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Bridge`: `L` is a finite extension of `ℚ_[p]` (a field with a
finite-dimensional `ℚ_[p]`-algebra structure and a compatible `ℤ_[p]`-algebra structure), normed by
its spectral norm; `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`; `R^×` is the image of its unit group;
`e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]` for a prime `P` over `pℤ_p` (unique, `padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal`).
The topology on `L` is that of the spectral norm and the measurable structure is `borel L`, both
supplied by `letI` inside each statement; every statement holds for every additive Haar measure.
`μ^log` is `IUT.Prerequisites.PadicVolume.padicMuLog`, normalized at `R`, and on a packet
`K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂` it is `padicPacketMuLog`, normalized at `(R_E)^∼ = padicPacketNormalization`.
Pages 9 and 13 take the tensor products over `ℤ_p`; for fields `K₁ ⊗[ℤ_p] K₂` and `K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂`
agree, the `ℚ_p` form is used here, and that identification is not formalized. The packet
statements take `K₁` and `K₂` in one universe.

## What is proved

1. *One finite extension, no norm hypothesis.* `volBridge_measure_smul`: `μ (y • A) = ‖y‖ ^ d μ A`
   for every `y ≠ 0` of `L` (`d = [L : ℚ_p]`), from the value group `p ^ (ℤ / e)`
   (`volBridge_norm_pow_ramificationIdx`). `volBridge_muLog_integralClosure`: `R` has positive
   finite Haar measure, `μ^log(R) = 0` and `μ^log(p · R) = −log p` (Proposition 1.4 (i) for one
   field). `volBridge_muLog_smul`: `μ^log(y • A) = μ^log(A) + log ‖y‖`.
   `volBridge_muLog_fractionalIdeal`: for `λ = k / e` and any `y` with `ord(y) = λ`, the fractional
   ideal `p ^ λ · R = y · R` has `μ^log(p ^ λ · R) = −λ log p`; `volBridge_muLog_uniformizer_zpow`:
   `μ^log(ϖ ^ k · R) = −(k / e) log p` for every generator `ϖ` of `P`.
   `volBridge_muLog_logUnit_bounds`, `volBridge_muLog_logShell_bounds`: the bounds
   `−a log p ≤ μ^log(log_p(R^×)) ≤ b log p` and the log-shell bounds, with `a`, `b` the constants
   of page 10 at `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`.
2. *An exact value.* `volBridge_muLog_logUnit_eq_of_le`: for `p > 2` and `e ≤ p − 2`,
   `μ^log(log_p(R^×)) = −(1 / e) log p`. This agrees with Proposition 1.4 (ii) exactly when
   `m = 0`; that `m = 0` under these hypotheses (no element of order `p` in `R^×`) is proved in
   `UnitVolume.lean` (`unitVol_card_torsion_of_le`), where `m` and `f` are defined.
3. *Tensor packets of two factors.* `volBridge_tensor_isReduced`: `K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂` is reduced
   (Mathlib: separable extensions are formally unramified, `Algebra.FormallyUnramified.base_change`,
   `.comp`, `.isReduced_of_field`). `volBridge_tensor_equiv_pi`: it is isomorphic, as a
   `ℚ_p`-algebra, to a finite product of finite separable extensions of `ℚ_p`
   (`Algebra.FormallyEtale.iff_exists_algEquiv_prod`). `volBridge_padicVolIntegral_iff`: the
   integrality of `padicVolIntegral` is the closed unit ball of the spectral norm, so the closed
   unit ball model and the integral closure model of `R_i` agree for the packet definitions;
   `volBridge_padicVolIntegral_pi`: integrality in a finite product is componentwise.
   `volBridge_packetNormalization_isCompact_isOpen`: `(R_E)^∼` is compact and open in coordinates
   (it is the preimage of the product of the closed unit balls). `volBridge_packet_muLog_normalization`:
   it has positive finite Haar measure, `μ^log((R_E)^∼) = 0` and `μ^log(p · (R_E)^∼) = −log p`,
   Proposition 1.4 (i) for `E` of cardinality two, on the object of page 9.

## Not proved

* That `(R_E)^∼` is a finitely generated `ℤ_p`-module spanning `K₁ ⊗ K₂` (a lattice); only
  compactness and openness are proved, which is what the normalization needs; it is proved for
  any finite number of factors in `Packets.lean` (`packet_normalization_lattice_tensor`).
* That `R_E` has positive Haar measure, so the step `μ^log(R_I) ≤ μ^log((R_I)^∼) = 0` of page 14
  is not obtained; the sublattice index formula.
* That `padicPacketNormalization` is the normalization of `R_E` in its ring of fractions (that the
  total ring of fractions of `R_E` is `K₁ ⊗ K₂`); it is the integral closure of `ℤ_p` there.
* Proposition 1.1, `p ^ (𝔡_{I*}) · (R_I)^∼ ⊆ R_I`, here; it is proved for two factors in
  `TensorDifferent.lean`. Proposition 1.2 (ii) to (iv) (of (ii), only the first display of its
  proof is in `TensorDifferent.lean`) and the inequalities of Proposition 1.4 (iii), (iv) remain
  open.
* Proposition 1.4 (ii) in general here; it is proved in `UnitVolume.lean`
  (`unitVol_muLog_logUnit_eq`).
* The weighting of `μ^log` over the factors of the decomposition and the additivity used on
  page 14; packets of any finite number of factors are decomposed and normalized in
  `Packets.lean`.
-/

open MeasureTheory Measure IUT.Prerequisites.PadicVolume
open scoped Pointwise

namespace IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields

section Field

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] (L : Type*) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ_[p] L]
  [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] L] [Algebra ℤ_[p] L] [IsScalarTower ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] L]

/-- For every nonzero `y` of a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_[p]` with its spectral norm,
`‖y‖ ^ e = p ^ (-k)` for an integer `k`, with `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`: the value group is
`p ^ (ℤ / e)`. -/
theorem volBridge_norm_pow_ramificationIdx (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] {y : L} (hy : y ≠ 0) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ∃ k : ℤ, ‖y‖ ^ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] = (p : ℝ) ^ (-k) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, -, -, hpe, hval, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hval y hy
  refine ⟨k, ?_⟩
  rw [hk, ← zpow_natCast, ← zpow_mul, mul_comm, zpow_mul, zpow_natCast, hpe, inv_zpow', zpow_neg]

/-- **Scaling of Haar measure by any element of `L`**: for a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_[p]` with
its spectral norm and the Borel structure, every additive Haar measure `μ`, every `y ≠ 0` in `L`
and every set `A`, `μ (y • A) = ‖y‖ ^ d · μ A` with `d = [L : ℚ_p]`. No hypothesis on `‖y‖`
remains. -/
theorem volBridge_measure_smul {y : L} (hy : y ≠ 0) (A : Set L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      μ (y • A) = ((‖y‖₊ ^ Module.finrank ℚ_[p] L : NNReal) : ENNReal) * μ A := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  have : BorelSpace L := ⟨rfl⟩
  intro μ _
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  have := padicBridge_maximalIdeal_liesOver p L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  set M := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)
  have he : 0 < M.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) M
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := volBridge_norm_pow_ramificationIdx p L M hy
  exact padicVol_field_measure_smul p μ hy he hk A

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.4 (i) for one finite extension** (page 13), on the ring of integers
`R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` itself: `R` has positive finite Haar measure, and the normalized
log-volume `μ^log = log (μ (−) / μ R) / [L : ℚ_p]` satisfies `μ^log(R) = 0` and
`μ^log(p · R) = −log p`. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_integralClosure :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) ≠ 0 ∧ μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) ≠ ⊤ ∧
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) = 0 ∧
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L)
        ((p : ℚ_[p]) • (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L)) = -Real.log p := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  have : BorelSpace L := ⟨rfl⟩
  intro μ _
  rw [padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall p L]
  exact ⟨padicVol_unitBall_ne_zero p μ, padicVol_unitBall_ne_top p μ, padicMuLog_unitBall p μ,
    padicMuLog_p_smul_unitBall p μ⟩

/-- **Scaling of the normalized log-volume by any element of `L`**: for `y ≠ 0` and `A` of
positive finite Haar measure, `μ^log(y • A) = μ^log(A) + log ‖y‖`, normalized at
`R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_smul {y : L} (hy : y ≠ 0) (A : Set L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure], μ A ≠ 0 → μ A ≠ ⊤ →
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (y • A) =
        padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) A + Real.log ‖y‖ := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  have : BorelSpace L := ⟨rfl⟩
  intro μ _ hA0 hA
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  have := padicBridge_maximalIdeal_liesOver p L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  set M := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)
  have he : 0 < M.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) M
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := volBridge_norm_pow_ramificationIdx p L M hy
  rw [padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall p L]
  exact padicMuLog_field_smul p μ hy he hk hA0 hA

omit [Algebra ℚ_[p] L] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] L] [IsScalarTower ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] L] in
/-- The fractional ideal `y · R` generated by `y ≠ 0` over `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` is
`y • R` as a set. -/
theorem volBridge_range_mul_eq_smul (y : L) :
    Set.range (fun r : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => y * (r : L)) =
      y • (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) := by
  ext z
  simp only [Set.mem_range, Set.mem_smul_set, SetLike.mem_coe, smul_eq_mul]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨r, hr⟩ => ⟨r, r.2, hr⟩, fun ⟨r, hr, h⟩ => ⟨⟨r, hr⟩, h⟩⟩

/-- **`μ^log` of a fractional ideal** (the scaling rule behind the computations of IUT IV pages 13
and 14): for `λ = k / e ∈ (1 / e) ℤ`, `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`, and any `y` with
`ord(y) = λ` (that is `‖y‖ = p ^ (−λ)`), the fractional ideal `p ^ λ · R = y · R` has
`μ^log(p ^ λ · R) = −λ log p`. Such `y` exist by `padicBridge_exists_norm_eq_rpow`. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_fractionalIdeal (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] (k : ℤ) {y : L} :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ‖y‖ = (p : ℝ) ^ (-((k : ℝ) / P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p])) →
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L)
          (Set.range (fun r : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => y * (r : L))) =
        -((k : ℝ) / P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]) * Real.log p := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  intro hy μ _
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hy0 : y ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0, norm_zero] at hy
    exact (Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hp0 _).ne' hy.symm
  obtain ⟨hR0, hR1, hR, -⟩ := volBridge_muLog_integralClosure p L μ
  rw [volBridge_range_mul_eq_smul, volBridge_muLog_smul p L hy0 _ μ hR0 hR1, hR, zero_add, hy,
    Real.log_rpow hp0]

/-- **`μ^log(ϖ ^ k · R) = −(k / e) log p`** for every generator `ϖ` of the prime `P` over `p`
(a uniformizer of `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`), every `k ∈ ℤ`, and
`e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_uniformizer_zpow (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] {ϖ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L}
    (hϖ : P = Ideal.span {ϖ}) (k : ℤ) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L)
          (Set.range (fun r : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => (ϖ : L) ^ k * (r : L))) =
        -((k : ℝ) / P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]) * Real.log p := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  intro μ _
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  obtain ⟨ϖ₀, -, h₀, -, hpos, -, hpe, -, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  have hassoc : Associated ϖ ϖ₀ := Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton.mp (hϖ.symm.trans h₀)
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hassoc
  have hnorm : ‖(ϖ : L)‖ = ‖(ϖ₀ : L)‖ := by
    rw [← hu]
    push_cast
    rw [norm_mul, (padicBridge_isUnit_iff p L _).1 u.isUnit, mul_one]
  have he : P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≠ 0 :=
    (ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P).ne'
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hr := padicBridge_rpow_of_pow_eq p hpos.le he hpe
  apply volBridge_muLog_fractionalIdeal p L P k
  rw [norm_zpow, hnorm, hr, ← Real.rpow_intCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hp0.le]
  congr 1
  ring

/-- **Bounds for `μ^log(log_p(R^×))` from IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i)** (pages 10 and 11) on the
paper's objects: `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`, `R^×` its unit group, `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`
and `a`, `b` the constants of page 10:
`−a · log p ≤ μ^log(log_p(R^×)) ≤ b · log p`. No hypothesis on the norm remains. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_logUnit_bounds (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      -Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]) * Real.log p ≤
          padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogUnit '' Set.range
            (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L))) ∧
        padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogUnit '' Set.range
            (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L))) ≤
          Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]) * Real.log p := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  have : BorelSpace L := ⟨rfl⟩
  intro μ _
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have he : 1 ≤ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, -, -, hpe, -, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  rw [padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall p L, padicBridge_range_units_eq_unitSphere p L]
  exact padicMuLog_logUnit_bounds p μ he (padicBridge_hval p L P) hpe

/-- **Bounds for the log-shell** `I = (p*)⁻¹ · log_p(R^×)` (IUT III Definition 1.1, as
`extLogShell`), from IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i), on the paper's objects as in
`volBridge_muLog_logUnit_bounds`: `μ^log(I) = μ^log(log_p(R^×)) + log p*` and
`−a · log p + log p* ≤ μ^log(I) ≤ b · log p + log p*`. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_logShell_bounds (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogShell p L) =
          padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogUnit '' Set.range
            (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L))) +
            Real.log (IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogPStar p) ∧
        -Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]) * Real.log p +
            Real.log (IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogPStar p) ≤
          padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogShell p L) ∧
        padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogShell p L) ≤
          Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]) * Real.log p +
            Real.log (IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogPStar p) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  have : BorelSpace L := ⟨rfl⟩
  intro μ _
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have he : 1 ≤ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, -, -, hpe, -, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  rw [padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall p L, padicBridge_range_units_eq_unitSphere p L]
  exact padicMuLog_logShell_bounds p μ he (padicBridge_hval p L P) hpe

/-- **The exact value of `μ^log(log_p(R^×))` when `p > 2` and `e ≤ p − 2`**: with
`R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` and `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`,
`μ^log(log_p(R^×)) = −(1 / e) log p`, from the equality case `log_p(R^×) = p ^ (1 / e) · R` of
Proposition 1.2 (i). This is the value `−(1 / e + m / (e f)) log p` of Proposition 1.4 (ii) when
`m = 0`; that `m = 0` in this case is proved in `UnitVolume.lean`. -/
theorem volBridge_muLog_logUnit_eq_of_le (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] (hp2 : 2 < p)
    (hep : P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≤ p - 2) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
    letI : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
    ∀ (μ : Measure L) [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure],
      padicMuLog p μ (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Set L) (extLogUnit '' Set.range
          (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L))) =
        -(1 / (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] : ℝ)) * Real.log p := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  let _ : MeasurableSpace L := borel L
  have : BorelSpace L := ⟨rfl⟩
  intro μ _
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have he : 1 ≤ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, hpos, -, hpe, -, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  have hr := padicBridge_rpow_of_pow_eq p hpos.le (by omega) hpe
  rw [padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_eq_of_le p L P hp2 hep, ← hr,
    padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall p L]
  have h := padicMuLog_ball_uniformizer p μ he hpe 1
  rw [zpow_one] at h
  rw [h]
  push_cast
  ring

end Field

/-! ## Tensor packets -/

section Packet

universe u

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime]

/-- **The two models of `R_i` agree**: for a finite extension `A` of `ℚ_[p]`, an element is
integral over `ℤ_p` in the sense of `padicVolIntegral` (used for `R_E` and `(R_E)^∼` in
`IUT.Prerequisites.PadicVolume`) if and only if its spectral norm is at most one. -/
theorem volBridge_padicVolIntegral_iff (A : Type*) [Field A] [Algebra ℚ_[p] A]
    [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] A] (x : A) :
    padicVolIntegral p x ↔ spectralNorm ℚ_[p] A x ≤ 1 := by
  let _ : Algebra ℤ_[p] A := ((algebraMap ℚ_[p] A).comp (algebraMap ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p])).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] A := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl
  exact (padicBridge_norm_le_one_iff_isIntegral p A x).symm

/-- **Integrality in a finite product**: an element of `Π i, A i` is integral over `ℤ_p` if and
only if every component is. -/
theorem volBridge_padicVolIntegral_pi {I : Type*} [Fintype I] (A : I → Type*)
    [∀ i, CommRing (A i)] [∀ i, Algebra ℚ_[p] (A i)] (x : Π i, A i) :
    padicVolIntegral p x ↔ ∀ i, padicVolIntegral p (x i) := by
  constructor
  · intro h i
    exact padicVolIntegral_map p (Pi.evalAlgHom ℚ_[p] A i) h
  · intro h
    choose P hP h0 using h
    refine ⟨∏ i, P i, Polynomial.monic_prod_of_monic _ _ fun i _ => hP i, ?_⟩
    funext i
    show Pi.evalRingHom A i (Polynomial.eval₂ _ x (∏ j, P j)) = 0
    rw [Polynomial.hom_eval₂, ← Polynomial.coe_eval₂RingHom, map_prod]
    have hc : (Pi.evalRingHom A i).comp
        ((algebraMap ℚ_[p] (Π i, A i)).comp (algebraMap ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p])) =
        (algebraMap ℚ_[p] (A i)).comp (algebraMap ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p]) := RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl
    rw [hc]
    exact Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ i) (h0 i)

/-- Tensor products of finite extensions are formally unramified over `ℚ_p` (characteristic zero,
so both factors are separable). -/
theorem volBridge_tensor_formallyUnramified (K₁ K₂ : Type*) [Field K₁] [Field K₂]
    [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₁] [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₂] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₁]
    [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₂] :
    Algebra.FormallyUnramified ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) := by
  have : Algebra.FormallyUnramified ℚ_[p] K₂ := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.of_isSeparable _ _
  have : Algebra.FormallyUnramified ℚ_[p] K₁ := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.of_isSeparable _ _
  exact Algebra.FormallyUnramified.comp ℚ_[p] K₁ _

/-- **`K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂` is reduced** for finite extensions `K₁`, `K₂` of `ℚ_p`. -/
theorem volBridge_tensor_isReduced (K₁ K₂ : Type*) [Field K₁] [Field K₂] [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₁]
    [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₂] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₁] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₂] :
    IsReduced (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) := by
  have := volBridge_tensor_formallyUnramified p K₁ K₂
  exact Algebra.FormallyUnramified.isReduced_of_field ℚ_[p] _

/-- **`K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂` is a finite product of finite separable extensions of `ℚ_p`** (the
decomposition "as direct sums of finitely many finite extensions of `ℚ_p`" of IUT IV page 13). -/
theorem volBridge_tensor_equiv_pi (K₁ K₂ : Type u) [Field K₁] [Field K₂] [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₁]
    [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₂] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₁] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₂] :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : Fintype I) (A : I → Type u) (_ : ∀ i, Field (A i))
      (_ : ∀ i, Algebra ℚ_[p] (A i)) (_ : TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂ ≃ₐ[ℚ_[p]] Π i, A i),
      ∀ i, Algebra.IsSeparable ℚ_[p] (A i) ∧ FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] (A i) := by
  have := volBridge_tensor_formallyUnramified p K₁ K₂
  have hE : Algebra.FormallyEtale ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) :=
    Algebra.FormallyEtale.iff_formallyUnramified_of_field.mpr this
  obtain ⟨I, hI, A, hF, hA, e, hs⟩ :=
    (Algebra.FormallyEtale.iff_exists_algEquiv_prod ℚ_[p] _).mp hE
  classical
  refine ⟨I, Fintype.ofFinite I, A, hF, hA, e, fun i => ⟨hs i, ?_⟩⟩
  refine Module.Finite.of_surjective ((Pi.evalAlgHom ℚ_[p] A i).comp e.toAlgHom).toLinearMap ?_
  intro y
  exact ⟨e.symm (Pi.single i y), by simp⟩

/-- **`(R_E)^∼` is compact and open** (for two factors): in the coordinates of
`Module.finBasis` used by `padicPacketMuLog`, the set `padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂` of
elements of `K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂` integral over `ℤ_p` is compact and open. It is the preimage of the
product of the closed unit balls under the decomposition `volBridge_tensor_equiv_pi`. -/
theorem volBridge_packetNormalization_isCompact_isOpen (K₁ K₂ : Type u) [Field K₁] [Field K₂]
    [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₁] [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₂] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₁]
    [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₂] :
    IsCompact ((Module.finBasis ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).equivFun ''
        padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) ∧
      IsOpen ((Module.finBasis ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).equivFun ''
        padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) := by
  obtain ⟨I, _, A, _, _, e, hA⟩ := volBridge_tensor_equiv_pi p K₁ K₂
  have : ∀ i, FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] (A i) := fun i => (hA i).2
  let _ : ∀ i, NormedField (A i) := fun i => spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] (A i)
  let _ : ∀ i, NormedAlgebra ℚ_[p] (A i) := fun i => spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] (A i)
  set c := (Module.finBasis ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).equivFun
  let Φ := (c.symm.trans e.toLinearEquiv).toContinuousLinearEquiv
  have hΦ : ∀ z, Φ (c z) = e z := fun z => by simp [Φ]
  have hS : c '' padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂ =
      Φ ⁻¹' Set.univ.pi (fun i => {y : A i | ‖y‖ ≤ 1}) := by
    ext t
    simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_univ_pi, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ i
      rw [hΦ]
      exact (volBridge_padicVolIntegral_iff p (A i) _).1
        ((volBridge_padicVolIntegral_pi p A (e z)).1 (padicVolIntegral_map p e.toAlgHom hz) i)
    · intro ht
      refine ⟨c.symm t, ?_, by simp⟩
      have h1 : padicVolIntegral p (e (c.symm t)) := by
        refine (volBridge_padicVolIntegral_pi p A _).2 fun i => ?_
        refine (volBridge_padicVolIntegral_iff p (A i) _).2 ?_
        have h3 : Φ t = e (c.symm t) := by rw [← hΦ, c.apply_symm_apply]
        have := ht i
        rw [h3] at this
        exact this
      have h2 := padicVolIntegral_map p e.symm.toAlgHom h1
      have h3 : (e.symm.toAlgHom : _ → _) (e (c.symm t)) = c.symm t := e.symm_apply_apply _
      rw [h3] at h2
      exact h2
  rw [hS]
  have hB := fun i => padicVol_unitBall_isOpen_isCompact p (K := A i)
  exact ⟨Φ.toHomeomorph.isCompact_preimage.mpr (isCompact_univ_pi fun i => (hB i).2),
    (isOpen_set_pi Set.finite_univ fun i _ => (hB i).1).preimage Φ.continuous⟩

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.4 (i) for a two-factor packet** (page 13), on `(R_E)^∼` itself: for
every additive Haar measure `μ` on the coordinate space of `K₁ ⊗[ℚ_p] K₂`, the set `(R_E)^∼`
(`padicPacketNormalization`) has positive finite measure in coordinates, and the packet
log-volume normalized at it satisfies `μ^log((R_E)^∼) = 0` and `μ^log(p · (R_E)^∼) = −log p`. -/
theorem volBridge_packet_muLog_normalization (K₁ K₂ : Type u) [Field K₁] [Field K₂]
    [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₁] [Algebra ℚ_[p] K₂] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₁]
    [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] K₂]
    [MeasurableSpace (Fin (Module.finrank ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)) → ℚ_[p])]
    [BorelSpace (Fin (Module.finrank ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)) → ℚ_[p])]
    (μ : Measure (Fin (Module.finrank ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)) → ℚ_[p]))
    [μ.IsAddHaarMeasure] :
    μ ((Module.finBasis ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).equivFun ''
        padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) ≠ 0 ∧
      μ ((Module.finBasis ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).equivFun ''
        padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) ≠ ⊤ ∧
      padicPacketMuLog p (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) μ (padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂)
        (padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) = 0 ∧
      padicPacketMuLog p (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) μ (padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂)
        ((p : ℚ_[p]) • padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) = -Real.log p := by
  obtain ⟨hK, hO⟩ := volBridge_packetNormalization_isCompact_isOpen p K₁ K₂
  have h0mem : (0 : TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) ∈ padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂ := by
    show padicVolIntegral p (0 : TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)
    unfold padicVolIntegral
    rw [← RingHom.map_zero ((algebraMap ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).comp
      (algebraMap ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p]))]
    exact RingHom.isIntegralElem_map _
  have hne : μ ((Module.finBasis ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂)).equivFun ''
      padicPacketNormalization p K₁ K₂) ≠ 0 :=
    hO.measure_ne_zero μ ⟨_, Set.mem_image_of_mem _ h0mem⟩
  have hfin := hK.measure_lt_top (μ := μ) |>.ne
  have hD : 0 < Module.finrank ℚ_[p] (TensorProduct ℚ_[p] K₁ K₂) := by
    rw [padicVol_finrank_tensor p K₁ K₂]
    exact Nat.mul_pos Module.finrank_pos Module.finrank_pos
  have h := padicPacketMuLog_p_zpow_smul p μ hD hne hfin hne hfin 1
  rw [zpow_one, padicPacketMuLog_self] at h
  refine ⟨hne, hfin, padicPacketMuLog_self p μ _, ?_⟩
  rw [h]
  simp

end Packet

end IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields
